# Task: Add a splash screen, loading bar, "Press to start" and a colour-transition intro to Mimblumi

## Context

Mimblumi (`hiyroscript/mimblumi`) is currently one self-contained `index.html` (~1,120 lines):
- An inline `<style>` block with `--haze`, `--ink`, `--note-bg` and `--font-text: "Avenir Next", "Segoe UI", system-ui, sans-serif`.
- `<div id="stage">` (the Three.js canvas goes here) and `<p id="fail" hidden>` (the WebGL error note).
- Three.js r128 loaded from cdnjs, then one IIFE script. That script builds the world and ends with `start(saved)`, which builds the player, generates the first ring of chunks synchronously (`while (World.step())`), wires input/resize and starts `requestAnimationFrame(frame)`. `window.claude.hot` (`snapshot` / `ready` / `data`) is used for hot reload.

The intro must work the same way as the splash in my **Alva** repo (`hiyroscript/alva`). Read these files there first:
- `js/screens/splash-screen.js`: the sequence logic
- `css/splash.css`: the styling
- `js/config.js` → `CONFIG.splash`: the timings
- `css/base.css` → `--font`: the font stack

Copy Alva's behaviour and feel exactly, adapted to Mimblumi's single-file setup. Keep everything inside `index.html` (inline CSS + JS, no build step, no new frameworks) unless an image file has to live next to it.

