## Reduced motion
If `matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)')` matches (same as Alva):
- Logos appear without zoom and are each held for `reducedMotionHold` (1000 ms) before moving on.
- "Press to start" doesn't pulse (static at full opacity).
- The colour transition becomes a single short cross-fade (or a much shorter run through the colours) followed by the fade into the game.

## Hot reload (`window.claude.hot`)
Keep the existing `hot.snapshot` / `hot.ready` / `hot.data` behaviour. On a **hot reload with saved data**, skip the whole intro and start straight into the world at the saved position/zoom, so development isn't slowed down. The full intro only runs on a normal cold start.

## Robustness
- Use one run token and cancel all animations, timers and listeners together, like Alva's `run` / `active()` / `clear()`, so nothing leaks or fires twice.
- Errors inside a step must never leave the player stuck on a black screen. Always fall through to the game or to `#fail`.
- No layout shift: the logo stays exactly centred while the bar and "Press to start" appear under it. Respect safe-area insets the way Alva does (symmetric padding `max(24px, env(safe-area-inset-*))`).
- Works on portrait mobile and desktop, in both light and dark system themes.
- Don't touch the world generation, rendering, shaders or gameplay logic beyond restructuring `start()` into loader tasks.

